{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And he went</b> ב\"ג המלך שבת תשובה וילך. Meaning: ב\"ג המלך — when Rosh HaShanah falls on day two or day three, then Nitzavim and Vayelech are read separately." "<b>And Moses went</b> Above it is written to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob, and adjacent to it is וילך משה — that he went to them to tell them that the Holy One, blessed be He, fulfilled His oath and brought Israel into the land. And it is found in the Midrash: from here, that the dead converse with one another."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "The acrostic phrase ב\"ג המלך שבת תשובה וילך is a calendar mnemonic; ב\"ג refers to days 2 and 3 of the week on which Rosh HaShanah can fall, determining when Nitzavim and Vayelech are separated."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:09.733250924Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}